      ],
      "title": "Friendship was invented in 18th-century Scotland",
      "gist": "Work gives what people need most, respect from peers for impersonal skills, and by loosening clan ties it freed friendship, so losing work threatens liberal individualism.",
      "question": "Work and meaning — why does work matter for dignity and for friendship?"
    },
